<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">18 June in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 18 June, from 618 to 1979.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">618</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Li Yuan proclaims himself emperor, founding the Tang dynasty</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After the fall of the Sui, Li Yuan took the throne at Chang'an as Emperor Gaozu. The Tang dynasty presided over one of the most brilliant periods of Chinese culture.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/tang-dynasty">Tang Dynasty</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changan">Chang'an</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1812</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">United States declares war on Britain</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Madison signed the declaration after Congress narrowly voted for war. The War of 1812 ended in stalemate in 1815, but gave Americans 'The Star-Spangled Banner'.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1815</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Wellington and Blücher defeat Napoleon at Waterloo</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The arrival of Blücher's Prussians broke Napoleon's final assault on Wellington's army near Brussels. Napoleon abdicated four days later and was exiled to St Helena.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1940</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">De Gaulle calls on the French to fight on</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Speaking on the BBC from London, General Charles de Gaulle rejected the coming armistice and urged French forces to continue resistance. The appeal founded the Free French movement.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/french-empire">French Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-de-gaulle">Charles de Gaulle</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1979</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Carter and Brezhnev sign the SALT II treaty</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The treaty capped each side's strategic nuclear launchers. The US Senate never ratified it after the Soviet invasion of Afghanistan, though both sides largely observed its limits.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a></div></li></ol>
